sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength on Archaeopteryx lithographica at 75 µm (Tithonian, 150.0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 83.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Periodic Schnakenberg system with a=0.112, b=0.836, Du=0.052, Dv=1.48, gamma=0.039, anisotropy 1.22, seed 3120. Analytical lambda_c = 11.991 cells, scaled so the physical wavelength is 7.478e-05 m (75 µm) at 150.0 Ma. Grid FFT wavelength is 12.00 cells (relative error 0.00072). Wing-transect Pearson r = 0.9803, nRMSE = 0.198, KS = 0.053. Equal-diffusion ablation std ratio = 0.00081. Gamma sweep is strictly decreasing. Predicted neighbor wavelengths at the same dx: Anchiornis 95.33 µm (160.8 Ma), Microraptor 57.05 µm (120 Ma). The Berlin-slab scan does not resolve 75 µm. Overall 83.5/100 (faithfulness 81.8, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 87, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/archaeopteryx_lithographica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-archaeopteryx-lithographica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 758256 B, 1496×924 px, artifact_sha256 4c1546e3a950825eaf079eeb0edd736a5e6177d9a95507f2a2b525cb01b4e166 (sha256 4c1546e3a950825eaf079eeb0edd736a5e6177d9a95507f2a2b525cb01b4e166), spec_fingerprint 6913098e47054812a2f1cf896b7e10fbf923735b2080ce927a3087eecb641c84. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6913098e47054812a2f1cf896b7e10fbf923735b2080ce927a3087eecb641c84; artifact_sha256: 4c1546e3a950825eaf079eeb0edd736a5e6177d9a95507f2a2b525cb01b4e166; input_dataset_sha256: {archaeopteryx_lithographica_berlin_slab.jpg=2e307a2774e08571..., archaeopteryx_lithographica_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=32deca0baa44c4ef...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator. | Schnakenberg 1979: kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Prum and Williamson 2002: within-feather bars and spots are a reaction-diffusion class. | Carney 2012: Archaeopteryx feather melanosomes at roughly micrometre length. | Manning 2013 and Foth 2014: plumage pattern and pennaceous feathers at 150 Ma. | Li 2010 and Li 2012: Anchiornis colour and Microraptor iridescence.; reconstructed_in_script: Parameter tuple (a, b, Du, Dv, gamma, anisotropy) chosen so lambda_c = 7.478e-05 m. | Gamma shifts 0.024 and 0.067 for the Anchiornis and Microraptor predictions. | Quartic plus three harmonics fitted to the wing optical-density transect of the slab scan.; transfer_boundary: The public-domain slab JPEG does not resolve 75 µm. The Pearson r is a scan-resolution transect fit, not a measured barbule spacing.; does_not_claim: That 74.78 µm was measured on this photograph. | That Anchiornis or Microraptor wavelengths were measured; they are gamma-transfer predictions. | A molecular identity for u and v.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'The wing overlay is too faint against slab contrast. Raise stripe contrast on the segmented vane and keep cv_sim_similarity >= 70.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Print the fundamental-only Pearson r (0.807) on the comparison figure next to the 3-harmonic r so the flexible fit is visible.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Annotate the segmented wing-mask fraction on the figure. Pass 1 leaves it only in fit_metrics.json.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.835"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

